      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>EndpointSubset is a group of addresses with a common set of ports. The expanded set of endpoints is the Cartesian product of Addresses x Ports. For example, given:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"  {\n    Addresses: [{\"ip\": \"10.10.1.1\"}, {\"ip\": \"10.10.2.2\"}],\n    Ports:     [{\"name\": \"a\", \"port\": 8675}, {\"name\": \"b\", \"port\": 309}]\n  }"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The resulting set of endpoints can be viewed as:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"  a: [ 10.10.1.1:8675, 10.10.2.2:8675 ],\n  b: [ 10.10.1.1:309, 10.10.2.2:309 ]"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Deprecated: This API is deprecated in v1.33+.</p>
      </dd>
